      en: ["Panchimalco was founded by the Pipil people before the Spanish conquest.", "The Santa Cruz de Roma Church dates back to the 18th century.", "The famous 'Festa de las Flores y Palmas' is held on the first Sunday of May.", "The town belongs administratively to the San Salvador Department.", "The elevation above sea level is approximately 590 meters.", "The name means 'Place of flags and shields' in the Nahuatl language."],
